cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Agent Passport
message: >-
  If you refer to Agent Passport in published work, please cite the
  specification. To cite the reference implementation in this repository
  specifically, use the software entry below.
abstract: >-
  An open standard for verifiable, business-issued identity and authority for
  AI agents that deal with other companies. A business publishes one signed
  JSON file at /.well-known/agent-passport.json declaring which agent acts for
  it, what that agent may do, how much it may commit, when a person takes over,
  and where the audit trail lives. The signing key is published in the
  business's own DNS, so a passport can be verified without a registry or any
  third party. The repository carries the specification, a threat model, a
  reference verifier, a command line tool and an MCP server.
type: software
